.\" Keep this page current: it describes the demo game demos/madrun2.bas (an executable made with BUILD, installed by "make install").
.TH ENGINE1999-MADRUN2 6 "November 2026" "Engine 1999 @VERSION@" "Engine1999 Manual"
.SH NAME
engine1999-madrun2 \- MADRUN II, a street crossing game for one to four players
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B engine1999-madrun2
.SH DESCRIPTION
MADRUN II is the second edition. New: a traffic helicopter of 4 x 3 sprites (a sprite group) with a translucent spinning rotor and a translucent shadow flies over the crossing now and then on a sprite path (you hear it when it comes), and pigeons walk about on the grass blocks on paths of their own. MADRUN is a crossing game for one to four players. A telephone is ringing in the open booth on the island in the middle of a busy crossing (sixteen rays run out from it so that you can see it from anywhere, and the receiver of the coin telephone jumps): get there before the caller hangs up. The first player there picks up the receiver, listens to the caller and talks, and hangs up, while the rest of the game goes on. Cars, trucks, buses, motorbikes and (later) ambulances drive on sixteen lanes (two in each direction on each of four roads); they stop for each other and for the crossings, but never for you. The four corners and the blocks between the roads are safe. If a vehicle hits you, you lie there for a moment, an ambulance drives in, takes you away and drives off, and only then do you start again in a corner. The first player at the booth scores the level (more points for a fast answer); every level has more and faster traffic, and a call you miss costs everybody a life. Pick-ups: a whistle stops the traffic for five seconds, boots make you fast for ten seconds, a heart is an extra life. A close call scores 5 points.
.PP
The program is the demo \fImadrun2.bas\fR of Engine1999, made into an executable with
.B BUILD
(window kind: it needs the SDL2 library, nothing else); its BASIC libraries are inside it. It opens the Engine1999 window; the window can
be switched between the full screen and a window with F11 or ALT+RETURN.
.SH CONTROLS
The game asks at the start for the keyboard (1 or 2 players) or for game controllers (up to 4: a controller that is connected brings its player, one that is removed takes it away).
.TP
.B Keyboard
player 1 moves with W A S D (with one player the cursor keys work, too), player 2 with the cursor keys.
.TP
.B Controllers
left stick or D-pad.
.TP
.B P
pause (START on a controller).
.TP
.B Q
quit (BACK on a controller).
.SH FILES
The high score is kept in the file
.I madrun2.hi
in the folder
.IR ~/.local/share/madrun2/
(the driver
.BR local: ;
the file is safe there and needs no permission; a file of that name in the current directory, where older versions kept it, is still read when the new one does not exist yet; the game goes on without the file if it cannot be written).
.BR engine1999\-basic (7)
has the details, see FILES AND DEVICES.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine1999 (1),
.BR engine1999-basic (7),
.BR engine1999-madrun (6)
